    <bpmn:process id="W_W537" name="W537. POS Card Terminal &amp; Acquirer Settlement Operations" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: End of cashier shift (batch close) or end-of-day store close (W5F); also triggered by card reader error or settlement exception
Frequency: Daily — per shift per terminal (3 terminals × 200 stores EOD + ~1 double-shifted terminal × 200 stores = ~800 batch closes/day)
Volume: ~1.0M card transactions/month (36% of 2.8M POS transactions); ~5,000 card transactions/store/month (~167/day/store)
Owner: Store Manager (settlement review); IT Operations (terminal troubleshooting)
Participants: Cashier (batch close), Store Manager (exception review), IT Helpdesk (terminal issues), Bank Acquirer (settlement processing)
Source: workflow W537 — POS Card Terminal &amp; Acquirer Settlement Operations</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W537_LaneSet5">
        <bpmn:lane id="W537_Lane1" name="Cashier">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W537_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W537_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W537_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W537_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W537_Start6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W537_Lane2" name="Store Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W537_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W537_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W537_Lane3" name="Finance">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W537_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W537_Lane4" name="IT Operations">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W537_Task14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W537_End15</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W537_Start6" name="End of cashier shift (batch close) or end-of-day store close (W5F); also triggered by…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W537_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W537_Task7" name="Card authorization at POS">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Card authorization at POS: during checkout (W5B.7), customer presents card; cashier or customer taps/inserts/swipes on PIN pad; POS system sends authorization request to acquirer via integrated payment gateway; system receives approval/decline with authorization code; transaction completed with card tender line on receipt
Responsible (R): Cashier / System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 5–15 sec per transaction</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W537_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W537_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W537_Task8" name="Contactless / QR payment">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Contactless / QR payment: customer taps contactless card or scans e-wallet QR on PIN pad for amounts below contactless limit (PHP 2,000); system processes without PIN; amounts above limit require PIN entry; e-wallet payments (GCash, Maya) processed via same PIN pad terminal using QR display
Responsible (R): Cashier / System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 3–10 sec</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W537_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W537_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W537_Task9" name="Shift-end card batch close">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Shift-end card batch close: at shift handover (W517), cashier or Store Manager initiates card batch close on each terminal; system transmits all authorized card transactions since last batch close to acquirer for settlement; acquirer confirms batch total (count + amount); batch close receipt printed and retained
Responsible (R): Cashier / Store Manager
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 2–5 min per terminal</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W537_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W537_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W537_Task10" name="Batch total verification">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Batch total verification: Store Manager compares card batch total on close receipt to POS card tender total from X-report (mid-shift) or Z-report (end-of-day); verifies transaction count and total amount match; flags variance &gt; PHP 100 for investigation
Responsible (R): Store Manager
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 5 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W537_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W537_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W537_Task11" name="Settlement exception handling">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Settlement exception handling: if batch close fails (communication error, acquirer timeout, total mismatch), system queues batch for retry; Store Manager contacts acquirer support if retry fails after 3 attempts; unsettled transactions held in terminal memory and retransmitted on next successful connection; exception logged per W48 (helpdesk ticket if IT assistance needed)
Responsible (R): Store Manager / IT Helpdesk
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 10–30 min per exception</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W537_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W537_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W537_Task12" name="PIN pad error troubleshooting">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: PIN pad error troubleshooting: if PIN pad malfunctions during transaction (offline, printer error, communication failure), cashier follows troubleshooting protocol: (a) restart PIN pad, (b) test with service card, (c) if persistent, log IT ticket per W265; cashier redirects card customers to adjacent terminal; if all terminals down, cash-only mode per W5E
Responsible (R): Cashier / IT Helpdesk
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 5–15 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W537_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W537_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W537_Task13" name="Daily settlement reconciliation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Daily settlement reconciliation: next-business-day, Finance receives settlement file from acquirer per W99 (payment settlement reconciliation); settlement file matched to POS batch totals; discrepancies (MDR fees, chargebacks, rejected transactions) flagged for investigation per FIN-037
Responsible (R): Finance / System
Accountable (A): Finance Manager
Duration: Per W99</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W537_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W537_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W537_Task14" name="Quarterly terminal inventory &amp; firmware audit">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 8: Quarterly terminal inventory &amp; firmware audit (per the Duration and staffing basis): IT Operations verifies all 600 PIN pads are online, running current firmware, and PCI-DSS compliant; firmware updates pushed during off-hours; non-compliant terminals flagged for replacement per W265
Responsible (R): IT Operations
Accountable (A): IT Manager
Duration: Quarterly</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W537_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W537_Flow26</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W537_End15" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W537_Flow26</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W537_Annotation16">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-264 (ensure controlled execution — Payment &amp; Cash Management (PA-08.2).) | - operational: automatic retry and terminal memory buffer; operational: next-day settlement file matching per W99
Owner: Store Manager (settlement review); IT Operations (terminal troubleshooting)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W537_Assoc17" sourceRef="W537_Annotation16" targetRef="W537_Start6" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W537_Flow18" sourceRef="W537_Start6" targetRef="W537_Task7" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W537_Flow19" sourceRef="W537_Task7" targetRef="W537_Task8" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W537_Flow20" sourceRef="W537_Task8" targetRef="W537_Task9" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W537_Flow21" sourceRef="W537_Task9" targetRef="W537_Task10" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W537_Flow22" sourceRef="W537_Task10" targetRef="W537_Task11" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W537_Flow23" sourceRef="W537_Task11" targetRef="W537_Task12" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W537_Flow24" sourceRef="W537_Task12" targetRef="W537_Task13" />
