    <bpmn:process id="W_W543" name="W543. POS Consignment Sell-Through Transaction Processing &amp; Vendor Settlement Trigger" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Customer purchases a consignment item at POS; consignment sell-through period settlement
Frequency: ~42,000 consignment POS transactions/month (~1.5% of POS transactions)
Volume: ~PHP 378M/month in consignment sales (~7.5% of in-store revenue)
Owner: Merchandising Manager (consignment terms); Store Manager (POS processing compliance)
Participants: Cashier (scanning), System (ownership transfer detection), Finance (vendor settlement), Vendor (consignment partner)
Source: workflow W543 — POS Consignment Sell-Through Transaction Processing &amp; Vendor Settlement Trigger</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W543_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W543_Lane1" name="Cashier">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W543_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W543_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W543_Lane2" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W543_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W543_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W543_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W543_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W543_Lane3" name="Finance">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W543_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W543_End12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W543_Start5" name="Customer purchases a consignment item at POS; consignment sell-through period settlement">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W543_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W543_Task6" name="Consignment item scan at checkout">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Consignment item scan at checkout: cashier scans consignment item barcode; POS system identifies item as consignment from item master flag (MDM — consignment indicator); system displays consignment indicator on cashier screen (discrete — not shown to customer); standard pricing and promotions applied per normal POS rules (W5B)
Responsible (R): Cashier / System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: No incremental time vs. standard scan</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W543_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W543_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W543_Task7" name="Consignment ownership transfer">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Consignment ownership transfer: at transaction completion (payment tender accepted), system executes ownership transfer for each consignment line item: (a) vendor-owned consignment inventory reduced by quantity sold, (b) standard owned inventory not affected (no owned stock existed), (c) ownership transfer event published via W533 with consignment flag, (d) COGS entry posted using consignment cost (not standard cost), (e) revenue posted per normal sales transaction
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W543_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W543_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W543_Task8" name="Consignment sell-through data accumulation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Consignment sell-through data accumulation: system accumulates daily consignment sell-through data per vendor: (a) item-level sales quantities and values, (b) date and store of sale, (c) transaction reference numbers; data published to vendor settlement accumulation table for FIN-018 processing
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W543_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W543_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W543_Task9" name="Consignment return processing">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Consignment return processing: when a consignment item is returned (W12), system reverses ownership transfer: (a) inventory returned to vendor-owned consignment stock (not BuildRight owned stock), (b) COGS reversed, (c) revenue reversed per standard return processing, (d) sell-through accumulation adjusted; if item is defective, system flags for vendor RTV per consignment terms rather than standard RTV
Responsible (R): System / Cashier
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: Per W12</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W543_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W543_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W543_Task10" name="Consignment pricing exception">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Consignment pricing exception: if vendor requests a temporary price change on consignment items (promotional pricing, markdown), pricing update flows through standard price push mechanism (POS-047) with consignment-specific GL posting (vendor-funded discount); Store Manager does not need to distinguish at POS — system handles automatically
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W543_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W543_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W543_Task11" name="Monthly vendor settlement trigger">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Monthly vendor settlement trigger: at month-end, Finance runs consignment settlement per FIN-018; POS sell-through data accumulated in W543.3 provides the settlement basis; settlement report shared with vendor for reconciliation; AP voucher created for vendor payment (consignment cost × quantity sold − vendor-funded discounts − defectives)
Responsible (R): Finance / System
Accountable (A): Finance Manager
Duration: Per FIN-018</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W543_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W543_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W543_End12" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W543_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W543_Annotation13">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-264 (ensure controlled execution — Payment &amp; Cash Management (PA-08.2).) | - operational: item master governance (W252) with consignment flag validation at SKU creation; operational: real-time consignment inventory deduction and vendor recall processing per W29; operational: transaction-level sell-through data (W543.3) as evidence
Owner: Merchandising Manager (consignment terms); Store Manager (POS processing compliance)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W543_Assoc14" sourceRef="W543_Annotation13" targetRef="W543_Start5" associationDirection="None" />
