    <bpmn:process id="W_W1268" name="W1268. E-Wallet (GCash/Maya) Daily Settlement &amp; Reconciliation" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: End-of-day store closing; daily e-wallet settlement window
Frequency: Daily per store (200 stores) + consolidated HQ review
Volume: ~420,000 e-wallet transactions/month (~15% of 2.8M total POS transactions); ~PHP 756M/month in e-wallet tender (~15% of PHP 5.04B in-store revenue)
Owner: Cash Office Clerk (store-level); Treasury Analyst (HQ reconciliation)
Participants: Cash Office Clerk, Store Manager (exception escalation), Treasury Analyst, Finance Analyst
Source: workflow W1268 — E-Wallet (GCash/Maya) Daily Settlement &amp; Reconciliation</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1268_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1268_Lane1" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1268_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1268_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1268_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1268_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1268_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1268_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1268_Lane2" name="Cash Office Clerk">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1268_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1268_Lane3" name="Treasury Analyst">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1268_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1268_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1268_Task14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1268_End15</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1268_Start5" name="End-of-day store closing; daily e-wallet settlement window">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1268_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1268_Task6" name="End-of-day e-wallet report generation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: End-of-day e-wallet report generation: at store closing per W574, system generates e-wallet tender summary per terminal and per store: (a) total GCash transactions — count and amount, (b) total Maya transactions — count and amount, (c) per-terminal breakdown, (d) any failed/declined e-wallet transactions during the day, (e) total e-wallet refunds processed
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1268_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1268_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1268_Task7" name="Cash Office Clerk verifies e-wallet totals">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Cash Office Clerk verifies e-wallet totals: Cash Office Clerk compares system e-wallet report (step 1) against POS e-wallet tender totals from Z-report (W574); flags discrepancies &gt; PHP 500 for Store Manager review
Responsible (R): Cash Office Clerk
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 10 min/store</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1268_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1268_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1268_Task8" name="System submits e-wallet batch settlement file">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: System submits e-wallet batch settlement file: POS system transmits end-of-day batch settlement request to each e-wallet provider: (a) GCash — batch sent to GCash merchant API with store ID, terminal IDs, transaction list, and total amount, (b) Maya — batch sent to Maya Business dashboard API with same data; system logs batch submission confirmation with reference number
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated (runs at 11:00 PM nightly)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1268_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1268_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1268_Task9" name="E-wallet provider settlement confirmation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: E-wallet provider settlement confirmation: by T+1 (next business day morning), e-wallet providers process the batch and: (a) credit BuildRight&#x27;s designated bank account with gross e-wallet collections minus MDR, (b) generate settlement report accessible via provider portal or API — showing: gross amount, MDR deducted, net settled amount, transaction count, any exceptions (duplicate charges, chargebacks), (c) system retrieves settlement confirmation via API or manual portal download
Responsible (R): System / Treasury Analyst
Accountable (A): Treasury Analyst
Duration: 15 min/day (HQ)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1268_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1268_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1268_Task10" name="Automated reconciliation — store level">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Automated reconciliation — store level: system matches: (a) POS e-wallet tender per store (step 1) vs. e-wallet provider settlement per store (step 4); (b) flags unmatched transactions (POS shows sale but no settlement confirmation, or settlement shows transaction not in POS); (c) calculates MDR per transaction and total MDR per store per provider
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1268_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1268_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1268_Task11" name="Automated reconciliation — HQ consolidation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Automated reconciliation — HQ consolidation: Treasury Analyst reviews consolidated e-wallet settlement dashboard: (a) total e-wallet collections per provider across all 200 stores, (b) total MDR fees deducted, (c) net settled amount vs. expected, (d) unmatched transactions by store, (e) exception summary (failed settlements, chargebacks, refunds)
Responsible (R): Treasury Analyst
Accountable (A): Treasury Manager
Duration: 30 min/day</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1268_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1268_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1268_Task12" name="Exception resolution">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Exception resolution: for each unmatched or disputed transaction: (a) Treasury Analyst investigates with e-wallet provider support (GCash/Maya merchant hotline or portal ticket); (b) common exceptions: (i) customer-initiated chargeback — verify with POS transaction log and CCTV timestamp, (ii) duplicate charge — refund via provider portal, (iii) settlement delay — track and follow up in 48 hours, (iv) QR scan failure where customer paid but POS didn&#x27;t record — reconcile manually with provider transaction reference; (c) unresolved exceptions &gt; PHP 5,000 escalated to Treasury Manager
Responsible (R): Treasury Analyst
Accountable (A): Treasury Manager
Duration: 30 min/day (as needed)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1268_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1268_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1268_Task13" name="MDR fee accounting">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 8: MDR fee accounting: system posts daily journal entries per store: (a) debit: bank account (net settlement received), (b) debit: MDR expense (merchant discount rate —GCash 1.5%, Maya 2.0% per contract), (c) credit: accounts receivable — e-wallet (gross e-wallet sales); monthly: Finance Analyst reconciles total MDR expense vs. provider MDR statements; MDR variance &gt; 0.1% of e-wallet revenue investigated
Responsible (R): System / Finance Analyst
Accountable (A): Controller
Duration: Automated + 1 hour/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1268_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1268_Flow26</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1268_Task14" name="Weekly e-wallet trend review">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 9: Weekly e-wallet trend review: Treasury Analyst reviews weekly e-wallet metrics: (a) e-wallet share of total tender (target: ~15%), (b) average transaction value by e-wallet vs. cash vs. card, (c) e-wallet settlement exception rate (target: &lt; 0.5%), (d) MDR cost trend, (e) provider uptime/downtime incidents; findings shared with Store Operations and IT for terminal health monitoring
Responsible (R): Treasury Analyst
Accountable (A): Treasury Manager
Duration: 1 hour/week</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1268_Flow26</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1268_Flow27</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1268_End15" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1268_Flow27</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1268_Annotation16">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-264 (ensure controlled execution — Payment &amp; Cash Management (PA-08.2).) | - operational: dual-provider strategy (if GCash is down, Maya may still work) and encouraging card/cash as backup
Owner: Cash Office Clerk (store-level); Treasury Analyst (HQ reconciliation)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1268_Assoc17" sourceRef="W1268_Annotation16" targetRef="W1268_Start5" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1268_Flow18" sourceRef="W1268_Start5" targetRef="W1268_Task6" />
