    <bpmn:process id="W_W1301" name="W1301. E-Wallet (GCash/Maya) Settlement Reconciliation &amp; Discrepancy Resolution" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Daily settlement reconciliation cycle; or e-wallet provider settlement delay &gt; T+2
Frequency: Daily reconciliation across 200 stores; ~420,000 e-wallet transactions/month (15% of total transactions)
Volume: ~2,100 e-wallet transactions per store per month; ~14,000/day chain-wide; average PHP 1,800/transaction (in line with the PHP 1,800 ATV, per W1268)
Owner: Treasury Analyst
Participants: Treasury Analyst, Store Cashier, POS System Administrator, E-Wallet Provider (GCash/Maya) Operations
Source: workflow W1301 — E-Wallet (GCash/Maya) Settlement Reconciliation &amp; Discrepancy Resolution</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1301_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1301_Lane1" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1301_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1301_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1301_Lane2" name="Treasury Analyst">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1301_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1301_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1301_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1301_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1301_End10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1301_Start4" name="Daily settlement reconciliation cycle; or e-wallet provider settlement delay &gt; T+2">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1301_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1301_Task5" name="Daily POS e-wallet transaction extraction">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Daily POS e-wallet transaction extraction: (a) system extracts all POS transactions with e-wallet tender type for the previous business day: transaction ID, store, terminal, timestamp, amount, e-wallet provider (GCash or Maya), authorization reference; (b) total POS e-wallet sales computed per provider per store per day; (c) system generates daily e-wallet transaction summary: total GCash transactions × amount, total Maya transactions × amount, grand total per store
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): Treasury Analyst
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1301_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1301_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1301_Task6" name="Settlement file matching">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Settlement file matching: (a) Treasury Analyst downloads daily settlement files from GCash Merchant Portal and Maya Business Dashboard; (b) settlement file contains: batch settlement amount, settlement date, number of transactions covered, gross transaction amount, fees deducted, net settlement amount; (c) system matches settlement batch to POS daily summary: (i) POS total gross e-wallet sales vs. settlement gross amount — expect match within PHP 100 tolerance (normal variance from voids processed after batch cutoff); (ii) if variance &gt; PHP 100: system flags for investigation
Responsible (R): Treasury Analyst / System
Accountable (A): Treasury Analyst
Duration: 30–45 min/day</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1301_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1301_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1301_Task7" name="Discrepancy investigation &amp; resolution">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Discrepancy investigation &amp; resolution: For flagged discrepancies: (a) Treasury Analyst compares transaction-level data: (i) POS transaction list vs. settlement transaction list (by authorization reference) — identify missing or extra transactions; (ii) check for voids/refunds processed in POS after settlement cutoff — these will appear in next day&#x27;s settlement; (iii) check for connectivity failures — transactions where customer&#x27;s e-wallet authorized but POS did not receive confirmation (result: customer was charged but BuildRight POS shows no payment — requires manual verification and journal entry); (iv) check for duplicate settlements — provider error settling same batch twice; (b) for unreconciled items: create investigation ticket with e-wallet provider&#x27;s merchant support with POS transaction details and settlement batch reference; (c) provider investigates and issues adjustment in next settlement or manual refund; (d) target resolution: all discrepancies resolved within 5 business days
Responsible (R): Treasury Analyst
Accountable (A): Treasury Analyst
Duration: 1–2 hours/day (on discrepancy days)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1301_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1301_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1301_Task8" name="Monthly e-wallet fee reconciliation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Monthly e-wallet fee reconciliation: (a) at month-end, Treasury Analyst reconciles e-wallet provider fees: (i) total fees deducted from settlements per provider vs. contracted fee rate × transaction volume, (ii) verify enterprise monthly flat fee billing vs. per-transaction fee calculation — whichever is more favorable per contract, (iii) identify any unauthorized fee rate changes by provider; (b) dispute any fee overcharges with provider; (c) post fee expense to GL: debit E-Wallet Processing Fees, credit Cash/Bank
Responsible (R): Treasury Analyst
Accountable (A): Finance Controller
Duration: 2–3 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1301_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1301_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1301_Task9" name="Store-level e-wallet operational support">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Store-level e-wallet operational support: When stores report e-wallet issues: (a) QR code not scanning: POS System Administrator checks terminal configuration and QR code display; (b) e-wallet payment failing: check if store&#x27;s internet connection is stable (e-wallet requires online connectivity unlike offline-capable POS); (c) customer claims payment was deducted but POS shows unpaid: Treasury Analyst checks provider portal for the authorization reference — if confirmed: process manual payment confirmation at POS and note for next day reconciliation; (d) weekly: POS System Administrator reviews e-wallet transaction failure rate per store — stores with &gt; 5% failure rate receive troubleshooting visit
Responsible (R): Treasury Analyst / POS System Administrator
Accountable (A): Treasury Analyst
Duration: Per incident + 2 hours/week</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1301_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1301_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1301_End10" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1301_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1301_Annotation11">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-184 (ensure POS settlement &amp; tender reconciliation completeness.) | - operational: Treasury Analyst review and approval gate; operational: periodic reconciliation against source documents
Owner: Treasury Analyst</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1301_Assoc12" sourceRef="W1301_Annotation11" targetRef="W1301_Start4" associationDirection="None" />
