    <bpmn:process id="W_W1467" name="W1467. Store Petty Cash Replenishment, Expense Tracking, Float Audit &amp; Custody Management" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Petty cash float drops below 30% of authorized limit; end-of-month expense reporting cycle; quarterly petty cash audit; or unplanned emergency expense
Frequency: ~2–3 replenishment requests per store per month; monthly expense report per store; quarterly physical audit of all 200 stores
Volume: ~400–600 replenishment transactions/month across 200 stores (PHP 20,000 float/store); ~PHP 5.6M–8.4M/month in petty cash expenses chain-wide (2–3 replenishments/store × ~PHP 14K+ restore)
Owner: Store Manager
Participants: Store Manager (custodian), Assistant Store Manager (alternate custodian), Cashier, Regional Operations Manager, AP Accountant, Internal Auditor
Source: workflow W1467 — Store Petty Cash Replenishment, Expense Tracking, Float Audit &amp; Custody Management</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1467_LaneSet5">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1467_Lane1" name="Store Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1467_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1467_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1467_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1467_Start6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1467_Lane2" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1467_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1467_Lane3" name="Cashier">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1467_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1467_Lane4" name="Internal Auditor">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1467_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1467_End13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1467_Start6" name="Petty cash float drops below 30% of authorized limit; end-of-month expense reporting…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1467_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1467_Task7" name="Disbursement">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Disbursement: (a) Store Manager (or Assistant Store Manager as alternate custodian) approves petty cash expenditure: (i) verify expense is within authorized petty cash policy (items &lt; PHP 2,000 per transaction; exclusions: payroll advances, personal loans, alcohol, tobacco), (ii) verify supporting receipt or invoice is provided; (b) Cashier processes disbursement from petty cash box; (c) system records: date, amount, payee, expense category, purpose, receipt reference; (d) for expenses &gt; PHP 1,000: Store Manager documents justification in system
Responsible (R): Store Manager / Cashier
Accountable (A): Regional Operations Manager
Duration: 5 min/transaction</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1467_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1467_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1467_Task8" name="Expense tracking &amp; categorization">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Expense tracking &amp; categorization: (a) system maintains running petty cash ledger per store: opening balance, disbursements (by category), running balance, replenishment received; (b) expense categories: maintenance supplies, office supplies, customer goodwill, transport/delivery, meals, emergency tools, other; (c) Store Manager reviews weekly: total disbursements vs. budget allocation, unusual spending patterns, receipts outstanding
Responsible (R): System / Store Manager
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 15 min/week</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1467_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1467_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1467_Task9" name="Replenishment request">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Replenishment request: When petty cash balance drops below 30% of authorized float (PHP 6,000): (a) system auto-generates replenishment request to AP; (b) Store Manager reviews outstanding disbursements, attaches all receipts, and submits replenishment request with: (i) total disbursements since last replenishment, (ii) receipts totaling disbursements, (iii) remaining float balance, (iv) requested replenishment amount = disbursements (to restore full float); (c) AP Accountant reviews: (i) receipts match disbursements, (ii) expenses within policy, (iii) no duplicate claims; (d) AP approves replenishment and initiates bank transfer or cash pickup per W541 deposit process
Responsible (R): Store Manager / AP Accountant
Accountable (A): Controller
Duration: 15 min/request</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1467_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1467_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1467_Task10" name="Replenishment receipt">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Replenishment receipt: (a) Cashier receives replenishment cash (from armored car pickup per W1354 or bank withdrawal); (b) Cashier counts and verifies replenishment amount matches approved request; (c) system records replenishment and updates petty cash balance to full float
Responsible (R): Cashier
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 10 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1467_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1467_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1467_Task11" name="Monthly expense report">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Monthly expense report: (a) Store Manager generates monthly petty cash expense report: total disbursements by category, receipt compliance rate, replenishment frequency, variance from budget; (b) Regional Operations Manager reviews store-level petty cash reports for policy compliance and spending anomalies; (c) AP Accountant reconciles petty cash expenses against GL store operating expense accounts
Responsible (R): Store Manager / AP Accountant
Accountable (A): Controller
Duration: 30 min/store/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1467_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1467_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1467_Task12" name="Quarterly physical audit">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Quarterly physical audit: Internal Auditor conducts surprise petty cash audit at sampled stores (~20 stores/quarter): (a) physical count of petty cash box — cash on hand + unreceipted vouchers must equal authorized float; (b) verify custody: petty cash box secured in safe, only authorized custodians have access; (c) review last 3 months of disbursements for policy compliance; (d) report findings to Controller; (e) any shortage &gt; PHP 500 investigated per LP exception process per W842
Responsible (R): Internal Auditor
Accountable (A): Controller
Duration: 1 hour/store</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1467_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1467_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1467_End13" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1467_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1467_Annotation14">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-264 (ensure controlled execution — Payment &amp; Cash Management (PA-08.2).) | - operational: dual-custodian (Store Manager + ASM) model with safe storage; operational: auto-trigger at 30% threshold
Owner: Store Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1467_Assoc15" sourceRef="W1467_Annotation14" targetRef="W1467_Start6" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1467_Flow16" sourceRef="W1467_Start6" targetRef="W1467_Task7" />
