    <bpmn:process id="W_W5566" name="W5566. Payment-Terminal Tampering &amp; Card-Skimmer Response (PIN-Pad Compromise Event)" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Discovery of a card-skimming overlay/shimmer/pinhole device on a PIN pad or payment terminal, a device with broken or absent tamper-evident seals or swapped hardware, a terminal missing from its assigned lane, or an acquirer/card-brand/PCI forensic alert naming compromised devices at BuildRight sites
Frequency: Rare but a standing industry threat: ~1–3 device-compromise discoveries chain-wide per year across the ~3,200-unit PIN-pad estate; organized skimming crews rotate through retail lanes, so the discovery cadence is unpredictable
Volume: 1 discovery × the terminal-fleet inspection sweep (200 stores × ~16 payment devices = ~3,200 units) × the card-present transactions at the affected lane(s) feeding the compromised-card assessment
Owner: Store Manager (site response); IT Operations (payment-device estate, forensics &amp; fleet sweep)
Participants: Cashier / Front-End Supervisor (first observers), Loss Prevention (CCTV preservation &amp; suspect-window analysis), Payment Operations Manager (acquirer &amp; card-brand liaison, W1205 PCI forensic engagement), Security Guard (lane closure &amp; device custody), VS-125 (compromised-card fraud watch), VS-91 (personal-data assessment where cardholder data was captured), Store Communications (VS-63)
Source: workflow W5566 — Payment-Terminal Tampering &amp; Card-Skimmer Response (PIN-Pad Compromise Event)</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W5566_LaneSet6">
        <bpmn:lane id="W5566_Lane1" name="Cashier">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5566_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5566_Start7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5566_Lane2" name="Store Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5566_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5566_Lane3" name="Payment Operations Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5566_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5566_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5566_Lane4" name="IT Operations">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5566_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5566_Task14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5566_Lane5" name="VS-91">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5566_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5566_End15</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W5566_Start7" name="Discovery of a card-skimming overlay/shimmer/pinhole device on a PIN pad or payment…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5566_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5566_Task8" name="Discovery &amp; freeze">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Discovery &amp; freeze: suspected device (bulky overlay, loose fascia, damaged seal, unknown pigtail) → do not remove or power-cycle beyond isolating the lane; photograph in place; close the lane; the device stays under security custody until IT Security/forensics release it
Responsible (R): Cashier / Front-End Supervisor
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: Immediate</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5566_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5566_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5566_Task9" name="Preserve &amp; escalate">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Preserve &amp; escalate: CCTV hold on the lane and approach paths per W838 covering at least 72 hours before discovery; note the last known-clean inspection from the W537 daily checks; escalate to IT Operations and Payment Operations Manager same hour
Responsible (R): Store Manager / LP
Accountable (A): IT Operations
Duration: Same hour</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5566_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5566_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5566_Task10" name="Notify acquirer &amp; card brands">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Notify acquirer &amp; card brands: device-compromise notification through the acquirer per the scheme&#x27;s PFI-trigger rules; engage the PCI forensic investigator through the W1205 program where card data capture is confirmed
Responsible (R): Payment Operations Manager
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 24 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5566_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5566_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5566_Task11" name="Fleet sweep">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Fleet sweep: chain-wide physical inspection directive — every terminal checked against seal/serial baseline, photographed, logged; stores confirm within the directive window; anomalies quarantine per Step 1
Responsible (R): IT Operations / Store Managers
Accountable (A): VP Store Operations
Duration: 48–72 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5566_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5566_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5566_Task12" name="Compromised-card assessment">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Compromised-card assessment: affected lane(s), dates and transaction populations compiled from W537 settlement logs and W1425 reconciliation; feeds issuer compromise alerts via the acquirer and the VS-125 fraud watch for presentment abuse
Responsible (R): Payment Operations Manager / VS-125
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 3–7 days</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5566_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5566_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5566_Task13" name="Privacy &amp; customer messaging">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Privacy &amp; customer messaging: where captured cardholder data is confirmed, route the VS-91 assessment (PAN + PIN is personal data under RA 10173; the W53 clock applies from confirmation); scripts for customer inquiries ready at the affected store
Responsible (R): VS-91 / DPO
Accountable (A): Data Protection Officer
Duration: Per W53</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5566_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5566_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5566_Task14" name="Retrofit &amp; after-action">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Retrofit &amp; after-action: tamper-evident seals and serial-baseline registry standing on the fleet; W537 daily checklist gains the seal/skimmer visual; LP briefing on the suspect pattern; inspection-sweep findings feed the W1205 evidence pack
Responsible (R): IT Operations / LP
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 2–4 weeks</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5566_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5566_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W5566_End15" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W5566_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W5566_Annotation16">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-264 (ensure controlled execution — Payment &amp; Cash Management (PA-08.2).) | - operational: payment devices are inspected against the seal/serial baseline daily (W537) and quarantined-in-place on suspicion; device-compromise notifications to the acquirer within 24 hours of discovery; fleet-sweep completion is evidenced per store before the event closes
Owner: Store Manager (site response); IT Operations (payment-device estate, forensics &amp; fleet sweep)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W5566_Assoc17" sourceRef="W5566_Annotation16" targetRef="W5566_Start7" associationDirection="None" />
